invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_post.h
catches: unit
reason: hspost_ticket_age_ok compares the age's low 32 bits alone, so a
  ticket about 49.7 days old or older reads as a young one and is offered.
  ch_cfg.ticket_age_ms is 64 bits wide so that no such age wraps. The row
  whose age is 2^32 + 5 milliseconds requires the refusal.

--- old
    return cfg->ticket_age_ms <= lifetime_ms;
--- new
    return (uint32_t)cfg->ticket_age_ms <= lifetime_ms;
